      "System.CreatedDate": "2026-09-07T20:27:03.013Z",
      "System.Description": "<p><b>Description:</b> Checkout is English-only, EUR-only, and offers cards and PayPal only, although the shop already ships to several EU markets. Checkout has not followed the international expansion. </p><p><b>Reason:</b> Sales wants five additional markets live this year. Support reports that non-English tickets already take days to resolve. Finance has no position on display currencies and FX pricing. There is no single owner for international checkout. </p><p><b>Implementation:</b> Scope is not defined: markets, languages, currencies, and local payment methods are all open. </p><p><b>For this story:</b> 1. Verify that checkout is usable when an international customer reaches it. 2. Verify that prices displayed in a non-EUR market are correct for that market. 3. Verify that an international order can be fulfilled like a domestic one when it is placed. </p><p>--- </p>",
